    "directions": [
      "Marinate the chicken with all the ingredients _except_ egg, cornstarch and rice flour. From here, you can proceed to the next stage immediately, or keep the chicken in the fridge until you are ready to fry!",
      "Just before frying, mix in an egg, and the cornstarch and rice flour (they equal 50 g in weight and are in the ratio 3:1). If your mixture is too runny, you may have to increase the flours a little in the given proportion.",
      "Drop each piece of chicken with a little mixture attached into 150°C oil. Fry on medium-low heat for about 6 minutes. Don't raise the heat or the chicken won't cook through. Drain over paper towels.",
      "You can eat these immediately, but if you want the pakoras extra-crisp, refry them in 180°C oil on high heat.",
      "Serve hot."
    ],
